  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Pavo Zubak is a Croatian automotive entrepreneur who founded AutoZubak and built a group spanning vehicle sales, servicing and roadside assistance. His companies distributed Volkswagen group brands and formed an import venture with Porsche. He later handed executive management to his son Ivan while becoming chairman of the family group’s supervisory board.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 96,
      "band": "very_high",
      "reason": "Contemporaneous trade coverage and company history establish the commercial development and management transition."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S1",
      "S3",
      "S5"
    ],
    "word_count": 52,
    "html": "<p>Pavo Zubak is a Croatian automotive entrepreneur who founded AutoZubak and built a group spanning vehicle sales, servicing and roadside assistance. His companies distributed Volkswagen group brands and formed an import venture with Porsche. He later handed executive management to his son Ivan while becoming chairman of the family group’s supervisory board.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Pavo Zubak grew up among seven children in Plehan, in Bosnia and Herzegovina. His father combined farming with metalworking, and initially expected him to learn a metalworking trade. Zubak instead chose to train as a motor mechanic, later continuing his technical education at Volkswagen facilities in Sarajevo and Germany.\n\nHe persuaded his father to sell the family property before they moved to Sesvetski Kraljevec in 1977. The workshop Zubak built opened the following year, with father and son as its employees. Decades later, he invited customers to criticise his company’s service through a prize campaign intended to gather their comments and suggestions.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 94,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Direct autobiographical interview supports the formative sequence; contemporaneous reporting separately supports the customer-feedback initiative."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S6",
      "S3"
    ],
    "word_count": 102,
    "html": "<p>Pavo Zubak grew up among seven children in Plehan, in Bosnia and Herzegovina. His father combined farming with metalworking, and initially expected him to learn a metalworking trade. Zubak instead chose to train as a motor mechanic, later continuing his technical education at Volkswagen facilities in Sarajevo and Germany.</p>\r\n<p>He persuaded his father to sell the family property before they moved to Sesvetski Kraljevec in 1977. The workshop Zubak built opened the following year, with father and son as its employees. Decades later, he invited customers to criticise his company’s service through a prize campaign intended to gather their comments and suggestions.</p>\r\n"
  },
